---
import ProviderPlaybookTemplate from '../components/ProviderPlaybookTemplate.astro';
const data = {
 "kind": "manage",
 "name": "cPanel (hosting)",
 "title": "How to Add and Manage DNS Records in cPanel (hosting)",
 "description": "Add, edit, and delete DNS records in cPanel (hosting) step by step, with the gotchas that break sites and mail, and free tools to verify every change.",
 "intro": "Managing DNS in cPanel (hosting) is a short walk once you know where the records live and which defaults to watch. This is the complete flow, with the verification step most guides skip.",
 "panel": "Your hosting account's cPanel, Domains section, Zone Editor. It manages the DNS zone for each domain on the hosting account, when your host runs the nameservers.",
 "steps": [
  [
   "Open Zone Editor",
   "cPanel, Domains, Zone Editor, click Manage next to the domain (or use the quick +A Record / +CNAME buttons)."
  ],
  [
   "Add the record",
   "+Add Record: name, type, TTL (14400 default), record value. Save."
  ],
  [
   "Watch defaults",
   "cPanel adds a webmail/autoconfig CNAME set by default; don't delete mail-related records if you use the host's email."
  ],
  [
   "Verify",
   "Record lookup for each record you added; hosting NS changes can take longer."
  ]
 ],
 "quirk": "Hosting providers often run cPanel AND the registrar role; changing nameservers at the host-registrar to their own defaults is usually a one-click preset.",
 "faqs": [
  [
   "Is cPanel DNS separate from my registrar?",
   "Yes: cPanel is hosting software. If your domain is registered elsewhere and pointed at the host's nameservers, cPanel's Zone Editor manages it."
  ]
 ],
 "related": [
  [
   "DNS record types reference",
   "/dns-records/"
  ],
  [
   "TTL explained",
   "/what-is-ttl-in-dns/"
  ]
 ]
};
---
<ProviderPlaybookTemplate data={data} />
